      "rows": [
        {
          "dimension": "Regulatory",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Storm's partial conviction on unlicensed money transmission established that U.S. prosecutors can hold developers liable for protocol-level transaction flows even without custody of funds, creating direct legal exposure for DeFi builders generally.",
          "source": "https://www.mayerbrown.com/en/insights/publications/2025/08/the-tornado-cash-trials-mixed-verdict-implications-for-developer-liability"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Sanctions",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "The 5th Circuit ruled OFAC's sanctions on immutable Tornado Cash smart contracts exceeded statutory authority, and Storm was acquitted on the sanctions evasion count, substantially undermining that prong of the government's theory.",
          "source": "https://www.bakerlaw.com/insights/victory-for-tornado-cash-as-court-rules-sanctions-were-unlawful/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Smart-contract",
          "level": "Low",
          "note": "Tornado Cash's on-chain contracts were never exploited; the entire legal risk arose from the protocol's use by sanctioned parties, not from code vulnerabilities or audit failures.",
          "source": "https://iq.wiki/wiki/roman-storm"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Centralization",
          "level": "Medium",
          "note": "Prosecutors argued Storm retained meaningful control through admin keys and governance participation; the defense maintained the protocol was fully non-custodial — this factual dispute was central to the hung money-laundering count and the retrial argument.",
          "source": "https://www.dlnews.com/articles/regulation/roman-storm-defends-running-tornado-cash-as-judge-weighs-acquittal/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Market / Chilling Effect",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "Developers publicly warned Congress and the Trump administration that prosecuting open-source privacy tooling would drive crypto innovation offshore, and Gusto's deplatforming of Storm demonstrated real-world professional consequences beyond the courtroom.",
          "source": "https://www.facebook.com/cointelegraph/posts/-update-more-than-65-advocacy-groups-have-asked-president-trump-to-drop-all-rema/1157112179928942/"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "Legal / Retrial Exposure",
          "level": "High",
          "note": "DOJ's pursuit of a retrial on the hung money-laundering counts, carrying up to 40 years in prison, left Storm's legal exposure unresolved well into 2026 despite acquittal on sanctions charges.",
          "source": "https://unchainedcrypto.com/doj-seeks-retrial-of-tornado-cash-developer-roman-storm-in-crypto-mixer-case-2/"
        }
      ],
